{"kind":"promise","text":"I will repair the cloned-repository how-to so its guards bind in the reader's shell.\n\nClaude's finding is right and I have re-verified both halves myself rather than taking the report on trust. internal/docset/examples_test.go:110 writes \"set -euo pipefail\\ncd \\\"$SCRATCH\\\"\\n\" ahead of every extracted block, and no block in the page sets -e itself — I checked the whole page, not only the cleanup block. So the two exact-path comparisons abort the script under make test and are no-ops in an interactive shell, while the comment at that block tells the reader a failed substitution \"stops the block instead of deleting\". The page states a safety property it does not have on the one machine where it matters, and a reader cannot discover that without reading our test harness. I ratified the verdict at 6943662d before promising.\n\nI will take the stronger of the two remedies claude offered rather than the honest one. Rewording the comment would make the page truthful about a guard that does nothing; adding set -e makes the guard real. The comment's attribution — that the comparisons and not find are the safeguard — is correct and stays as it is, because it becomes true rather than aspirational.\n\nOn the question claude could not answer, I found the sentence: line 260 of the page at bf589838 reads \"The second case is what to avoid, because gitseq has no merge for it.\" It is a claim the page makes, so I will address it in the re-review request rather than assert it does not exist.\n\nThe regression is the part I expect to be hardest and I will not pretend otherwise. Executing the extracted block WITHOUT the harness preamble is precisely what the current harness cannot do, so proving the fix needs a seam the docset package does not yet have. I will build the narrowest one that lets a test run one named block bare, and I will prove it by mutation at its own decision site: remove the in-block set -e and the new test must fail, restore it and it must pass. If that seam turns out to need a change to docset's contract rather than a test-local helper, I will stop and file a child request rather than widen this head on my own authority.\n\nConditions of satisfaction, as codex wrote them: set -e inside the reader-facing cleanup block before either guard; no rm, rm -f or rm -rf anywhere; unlink, rmdir, exact resolved-path equality and the comparisons-not-find attribution all retained; a mutation-sensitive docset regression that runs the block without the preamble and proves a failed guard leaves the target intact; the forked-sequence sentence clarified; gofmt, go build ./..., go vet ./..., git diff --check, go test ./... -count=1 and go test ./internal/docset/... -count=1 green at a clean pushed exact head; both live artifacts at docs/how-to/use-in-a-cloned-repo.md and docs/README.md superseded per succession; independent review requested naming both. I will not merge."}